# 13. Time and Space Complexity

Let:

```text
V = number of vertices
E = number of edges
```

## Time Complexity

```text
O(V + E)
```

Reason:

- Building the adjacency list takes `O(E)`.
- Calculating indegrees takes `O(E)`.
- Finding initial zero-indegree nodes takes `O(V)`.
- Every node enters the queue at most once: `O(V)`.
- Every edge is processed once: `O(E)`.

Therefore:

```text
O(V + E)
```

## Space Complexity

```text
O(V + E)
```

Reason:

- Adjacency list stores all vertices and edges.
- Indegree array stores `V` values.
- Queue can contain up to `V` nodes.
- Result list can contain `V` nodes.

